{
  "description": "Who holds the browser. seq rises by one with every change, and by says who made it. The agent hands the browser to the person with POST /sessions/{id}/control holder \"human\". Only the person hands it back, with Done in the browser, which records holder \"agent\" by \"person\". The API refuses holder \"agent\" with 403 person_only. A hand-over may name what it waits for, wait_for: {element, state \"checked\" or \"filled\"} or {page: \"changes\"}; a host that watches for it hands the browser back by itself once the person did it and left the page alone for a few seconds, recorded as their Done (holder \"agent\" by \"person\"), and says so with watching: true in its answer to the hand-over. An answer with watching false, or without it, means the host does not watch this hand-over, and only Done ends it. A host that does not know wait_for answers 400, and the agent hands over again without it. It never carries a value. GET /sessions/{id} answers even while the person holds control. since is epoch milliseconds. The session record also carries the active tab's title and url; url is null before a page loads. GET /sessions/{id} also says the most tabs the agent may open for the task (max_tabs) and the tabs a recycled session noted (parked_tabs: url and title), which reopen only when asked for.",
  "examples": {
